          "tipo": "gramatica",
          "min": 12,
          "titulo": "«Fazer», «dizer», «poder», «querer», «saber» and «pôr»",
          "explicacao": "STEP 1: these six verbs change their stem in the past: the vowel or consonant changes and the endings are -e / -e (without -ou) in the third person: «fiz, fez, fez, fizemos, fizeram». STEP 2: here are the six verbs in the past. «Fazer»: fiz, fez, fizemos, fizeram. «Dizer»: disse, disse, dissemos, disseram. «Poder»: pude, pôde, pudemos, puderam. «Querer»: quis, quis, quisemos, quiseram. «Saber»: soube, soube, soubemos, souberam. «Pôr»: pus, pôs, pusemos, puseram. STEP 3: the written accents matter: «pôde» (past, from poder) is different from «pode» (present). In the same way «pôs» (past) differs from «põe» (present). STEP 4: some of these verbs change meaning in the past. «Eu não pude ir» means I tried and could not go. «Eu soube» means I found out (I did not know and then I learned). «Eu não quis» means I refused. For the idea of wanting or knowing as a background situation you will use the imperfect in lesson 21: «eu queria», «eu sabia». STEP 5: «fazer» is used in the question «O que você fez?» (What did you do?). The answer repeats the verb or uses another: «Fiz o jantar.» or «Cozinhei.». STEP 6: derived verbs follow the same pattern: «desfazer» (undo) and «refazer» (redo) work like «fazer»; «pôr» also gives «compor», «propor» and «supor».",
          "comparacao": "English has the same kind of stem change in some verbs (make, made; say, said; put, put). The Portuguese list is longer, but it is a closed list that you learn once. The good news is that all these verbs share the same endings, with -e instead of -ou in the third person.",
          "exemplos": [
            {
              "ru": "O que você fez ontem?",
              "pt": "What did you do yesterday?"
            },
            {
              "ru": "Ela disse que chegou tarde.",
              "pt": "She said that she arrived late."
            },
            {
              "ru": "Eu não pude ir à reunião.",
              "pt": "I could not go to the meeting."
            },
            {
              "ru": "Eles fizeram a prova na sexta-feira.",
              "pt": "They took the exam on Friday."
            }
